  ],
  "description": "dbx 902, main board drawing 61100-000-01. Unbalanced input, engaged audio path and 10 kΩ line load. Both Frequency sections track the 20 kΩ reverse-log low-pass crossover; high pass is the full-band signal minus low pass. HF Only switches between broadband gain control and high-band-only reduction with the low band summed back. Two functional log-RMS detectors represent QA1 and QA2 with an estimated 4.7 ms power averaging time. The detector difference, Range bias, precision rectifier and control-voltage buffer drive a current-mode Blackmer VCA. The native THAT2180 equivalent uses unity-calibrated current input and a 6.1 mV/dB control interface in place of the original 202X module. TL07x models represent LF353/LF351 and the line driver uses equivalent closed-loop gain and output resistance. The OA6A/Q3 low-level detector shunt uses a continuous transition between the schematic comparator’s closing and opening thresholds. It returns gain to unity below the detector operating range. Trims are centered. Power filtering, LED metering and bypass are omitted.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Frequency",
      "Range"
    ]
  },
  "name": "dbx 902 De-Esser",
  "outputNode": "out",
